                <pb facs="0535" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">621.6217/5a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-01T14:00:00-04:00">June 1, 1935—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Department receiving complaints American exporters as to competition
                    encountered in Colombia from German exports facilitated by the use of
                    compensation or registered marks which do not have international acceptance and
                    which sell at a discount as compared with the official exchange value of the
                    Reichsmark.</p>
                <p>Would you please report immediately by wire and more fully by air mail upon the
                    recent development of trade relations between Colombia and Germany, paying
                    particular attention to any facilitation that may be given to this trade by the
                    Colombian authorities, and any special arrangements that may exist for the sale
                    of Colombian goods for blocked marks.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
